div.p:
—concentration of bilateral concessional assistance on the poor countries and the
                    use of concessional aid to support technological collaboration in the
                    middle-income countries and non-concessional aid to meet their other needs;

—a larger effort to mobilize the resources of the private sector, in both the US
                    and developing countries, to promote research, development, and training on
                    problems of direct concern to developing countries;
